# Force LF line endings on checkout for text files that must keep LF to work:
#
#  - *.patch: `git apply` matches context byte-for-byte; CRLF patches fail to
#    apply against the LF notcurses source (see tool/build_notcurses_windows_x64.sh).
#  - *.sh:    bash errors on CRLF (`$'\r': command not found`).
#  - native C headers/sources: matched by patches; must stay LF.
#
# Without these rules, a Windows checkout with core.autocrlf=true rewrites these
# files to CRLF and breaks the native build.
*.patch   text eol=lf
*.sh      text eol=lf
native/include/** text eol=lf
native/src/**     text eol=lf
